{"id":"3c1299db4f604d6f","group":"17","path":"17/17-thm-finite-ramsey.md","title":"Finite Ramsey Theorem","display":"thm-finite-ramsey — Finite Ramsey Theorem","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Model Theory (Chang & Keisler, 3rd ed. 1990)","book_abbrev":"17","label":"17-thm-finite-ramsey","aliases":["17-thm-finite-ramsey"],"display":"thm-finite-ramsey — Finite Ramsey Theorem","depends_on":["[[17-df-partition-relation]]"],"label_origin":"local-catalog","source_verification":"not-compared-to-book-in-this-pass; local statement reviewed","legacy_label":"17-thm-2.5.1"},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Model Theory (Chang &amp; Keisler, 3rd ed. 1990)"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"17"},{"key":"label","html":"17-thm-finite-ramsey"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>17-thm-finite-ramsey</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-finite-ramsey — Finite Ramsey Theorem"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"f06a70914e63dea9\" href=\"?note=f06a70914e63dea9\" title=\"17-df-partition-relation\">17-df-partition-relation</a></span></div>"},{"key":"label_origin","html":"local-catalog"},{"key":"source_verification","html":"not-compared-to-book-in-this-pass; local statement reviewed"},{"key":"legacy_label","html":"17-thm-2.5.1"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n,k,r\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\},\\quad n\\leq k\">\\(n,k,r\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\},\\quad n\\leq k\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcCombPartitionRelation}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcCombPartitionRelation}_S\\)</span> (partition-relation predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"f06a70914e63dea9\" href=\"?note=f06a70914e63dea9\" title=\"17-df-partition-relation\">17-df-partition-relation</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\forall n,k,r\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;\\Bigl(n\\leq k\\to\n\\exists N\\in\\omega\\;\n\\mathrm{ZfcCombPartitionRelation}_S(N,k,r,n)\\Bigr).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\forall n,k,r\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;\\Bigl(n\\leq k\\to\n\\exists N\\in\\omega\\;\n\\mathrm{ZfcCombPartitionRelation}_S(N,k,r,n)\\Bigr).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Equivalently, every <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"r\">\\(r\\)</span>-coloring of the <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\">\\(n\\)</span>-element subsets of a sufficiently large finite set has a monochromatic <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"k\">\\(k\\)</span>-element subset.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The side condition <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\\leq k\">\\(n\\leq k\\)</span> is required by the imported partition predicate, which defines monochromaticity by a color-image of cardinality exactly one. If <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"k&lt;n\">\\(k&lt;n\\)</span>, the family of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\">\\(n\\)</span>-element subsets of a <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"k\">\\(k\\)</span>-element set is empty and that image has cardinality zero. The conventional vacuous-homogeneity version covers these trivial cases separately.</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"17-df-partition-relation","status":"resolved","id":"f06a70914e63dea9","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[17-df-partition-relation]]","embed":false},{"target":"17-df-partition-relation","status":"resolved","id":"f06a70914e63dea9","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{ZfcCombPartitionRelation}_S$ (partition-relation predicate, see [[17-df-partition-relation]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"n,k,r\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\},\\quad n\\leq k","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ZfcCombPartitionRelation}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\forall n,k,r\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;\\Bigl(n\\leq k\\to\n\\exists N\\in\\omega\\;\n\\mathrm{ZfcCombPartitionRelation}_S(N,k,r,n)\\Bigr).","display":true},{"tex":"r","display":false},{"tex":"n","display":false},{"tex":"k","display":false},{"tex":"n\\leq k","display":false},{"tex":"k<n","display":false},{"tex":"n","display":false},{"tex":"k","display":false}],"bytes":1253,"backlinks":[{"id":"2c98c9e634ff4b44","anchor":"ref-180","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[17-thm-aleph-one-categoricity-consequences]]\n[[17-thm-atomic-model-existence]]\n[[17-thm-beth-definability]]\n[[17-thm-beth-definability-satisfaction-form]]\n[[17-thm-chain-sentence-preservation]]\n[[17-thm-chain-theory-preservation]]\n[[17-thm-compactness]]\n[[17-thm-compactness-equivalents]]\n[[17-thm-compactness-henkin-form]]\n[[17-thm-compactness-ultraproduct-form]]\n[[17-thm-completeness-characterization]]\n[[17-thm-countable-back-and-forth]]\n[[17-thm-countable-omitting-types]]\n[[17-thm-craig-interpolation]]\n[[17-thm-craig-interpolation-common-language]]\n[[17-thm-dense-linear-order-qe]]\n[[17-thm-diagram-embedding]]\n[[17-thm-downward-lowenheim-skolem]]\n[[17-thm-ehrenfeucht-mostowski]]\n[[17-thm-elementary-amalgamation]]\n[[17-thm-elementary-chain-union]]\n[[17-thm-elementary-diagram-embedding]]\n[[17-thm-erdos-rado]]\n[[17-thm-existential-preservation]]\n[[17-thm-extended-omitting-types]]\n[[17-thm-finite-ramsey]]\n[[17-thm-fraisse-limit]]\n[[17-thm-horn-axiomatization]]\n[[17-thm-horn-preservation]]\n[[17-thm-horn-sentence-characterization]]\n[[17-thm-horn-sentence-reduced-products]]\n[[17-thm-horn-theory-reduced-products]]\n[[17-thm-isomorphic-ultrapowers]]\n[[1